# REMOVED: Private key was hardcoded in this file and committed to version control.
# ACTION REQUIRED: This credential must be ROTATED (revoked and reissued) because
# the original key remains in git history and is considered compromised.
#
# To provide the TLS private key, use one of:
#   1. Set the environment variable TLS_KEY_PATH to point to an externally managed key file
#   2. Set the environment variable TLS_KEY_CONTENT with the PEM-encoded key value
#   3. Place a newly generated private key at this path (do NOT commit it — add to .gitignore)
#
# Generate a new self-signed key+cert for development:
#   openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout server.key -out server.crt -days 365 -nodes -subj '/CN=localhost'
